channels=''.join(f'<figure><div class="channel-image"><img src="results/00458u/channel-{c}.jpg" alt="{name} exposure of the locomotive" loading="lazy"><i></i></div><figcaption>{name.upper()} / {pos}</figcaption></figure>' for c,name,pos in [('b','Blue','TOP'),('g','Green','MIDDLE'),('r','Red','BOTTOM')])
for key,value in {'__OPTIONS__':options,'__MAX_TIME__':f'{max_time:.2f}','__CHANNELS__':channels,'__TRACE__':trace_rows,'__EXPERIMENTS__':''.join(experiments),'__CARDS__':''.join(cards),'__DATA__':json.dumps(data)}.items():html=html.replace(key,value)
html=html.replace('FIRST IMPLEMENTATION','BASELINE + OPTIONAL FEATURES')
html=html.replace('<div class="result-readout"', '<div id="viewer-features">'+feature_controls('viewer')+'</div><div class="result-readout"')
html=html.replace('Both sides use the same crop in the blue channel’s coordinates. Only areas without valid data in all three shifted channels are removed. Remaining coloured scan borders are intentionally visible in this baseline.', 'With all options off, compare unaligned RGB against the original pyramid NCC result. With an effect enabled, compare the original NCC result against your selected effects on exactly the same image area. Auto crop applies the detected rectangle to both sides for a fair comparison. Each photo remembers its own options while this page is open.')
html=html.replace('Every provided image, processed with the same settings. Switch the gallery view or select a photo to inspect it in the comparison viewer.', 'Every provided image, processed with the same settings. Use the checkboxes beneath each photo to combine optional effects. All options start off. Select a photo to inspect the original and edited versions above.')
html=html.replace('This baseline retains scan borders; automatic border detection, white balance, and colour correction have not been applied.', 'The original baseline retains scan borders. Optional crop detection and colour adjustments are now available below each photograph; they can be switched off independently.')
html=html.replace('Additional self-selected collection images and optional enhancements are still future work.', 'Five optional features now have reversible per-photo controls. Additional self-selected collection images are still future work.')
feature_section='''<section class="shell study feature-methods" id="features"><div class="section-heading"><span class="number">+</span><div><div class="eyebrow">BELLS & WHISTLES</div><h2>Choose what each photograph needs.</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Five independent options, 32 combinations per photograph. The original intensity-NCC images and measurements are preserved. White balance and colour mapping are hypotheses about appearance, not verified historical colours.</p><div class="discussion-grid"><article><h3>Gradient alignment</h3><p>Re-run the full-resolution pyramid with NCC on smoothed gradient magnitudes at each level, then apply the new shifts to the original channels. This emphasizes structure rather than raw brightness. The offsets shown below each image update when this option is selected.</p></article><article><h3>Automatic crop</h3><p>Detect row and column transitions near the image edges, supported by extreme brightness or inconsistent colour. A 15% search limit prevents deep cuts; it is not a fixed crop amount. If no convincing edge is found, that side stays unchanged. The detection overlay shows the measured rectangle.</p></article><article><h3>Gray-world white balance</h3><p>Estimate RGB means from the detected interior, excluding near-black and near-white samples; scale channels toward a shared mean. Gains are limited and a common exposure factor protects highlights. Scenes dominated by one colour can be overcorrected; leave this option off when it looks worse.</p></article><article><h3>Automatic contrast</h3><p>Stretch the detected interior’s 1st–99th percentile intensity range to [0, 1], using the same mapping for all RGB channels. This follows white balance when both are selected. Values outside the chosen range are clipped, so extreme details may be lost.</p></article><article><h3>Experimental colour mapping</h3><p>A fixed 3 × 3 matrix mixes each channel with 15% luminance, retaining 85% of chroma. Neutral colours stay neutral and saturation is gently reduced. Applied in encoded RGB, this is an aesthetic experiment, not a calibrated correction of the original filters.</p></article><article><h3>Reversible combinations</h3><p>Processing order: alignment → detected crop → white balance → contrast → colour matrix. Tone statistics exclude detected borders even when crop is off. Alignment is computed at original resolution; optional tone variants are web previews up to 1100 px. The original full-resolution downloads remain available.</p></article></div><div class="download-links"><a href="results/features.json" download>Feature parameters & crop bounds ↓</a><a href="../scripts/enhancements.py" download>Enhancement algorithms ↓</a></div></section>'''
html=html.replace('<section class="shell study discussion"',feature_section+'<section class="shell study discussion"')
html=html.replace('</body>', '<script id="feature-data" type="application/json">'+json.dumps(features)+'</script></body>')
(SITE/'index.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
